---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<!-- Site C · projects — case studies with context, outcome, and honesty -->
<BaseLayout
	title="Projects — Tarik Duyar"
	description="Things Tarik Duyar has built and runs: EgeceTV, REKV, Make2Game, Evrenomi, and a small fleet of servers."
	bodyClass="bg-[#0e1014] text-gray-300 antialiased"
>
	<main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
		<header class="mb-12">
			<div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-10">
				<a href="/13" class="flex items-center gap-3">
					<span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30 bg-blue-400/5 flex items-center justify-center">
						<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-300/80 text-lg leading-none select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
					</span>
					<span class="font-sinistre text-lg text-white">Tarik Duyar</span>
				</a>
				<nav class="flex gap-5 text-sm">
					<a href="/13/notes" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Notes</a>
					<a href="/13/projects" class="text-white underline decoration-blue-400/50 underline-offset-4">Projects</a>
					<a href="/13/now" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Now</a>
				</nav>
			</div>
			<h1 class="font-sinistre text-3xl text-white mb-4">Projects</h1>
			<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
				Not a gallery — a logbook. What each thing is, why it exists, and what
				state it's honestly in.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="space-y-6">
			<!-- EgeceTV -->
			<article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.015] p-7">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-gray-100">EgeceTV</h2>
					<span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80 border border-emerald-400/20 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">in production</span>
				</div>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What:</span> a health &amp; education
						streaming platform — my day job at Deniz Egece, where I'm the founding
						engineer. 17,000+ paying subscribers, ~1,000 videos, clients on web,
						iOS, Android, Android TV, and Apple TV.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">My part:</span> backend architecture, the
						MySQL schema, a single GraphQL API serving all five clients, the
						subscription payment system, and the CI/CD pipeline. When it breaks,
						my phone buzzes.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Honest state:</span> alive, growing, and
						teaching me daily that boring architecture wins.
					</p>
				</div>
				<p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-5">Next.js · GraphQL · MySQL · Prisma · AWS · GitHub Actions · 2022 — now</p>
			</article>

			<!-- REKV -->
			<article id="rekv" class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.015] p-7 scroll-mt-8">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-gray-100">REKV</h2>
					<span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-400/80 border border-blue-400/20 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">active development</span>
				</div>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What:</span> a type-safe key-value store
						library in Rust — memory-mapped storage, zero-copy deserialization,
						async I/O.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Why:</span> I use databases every day and
						decided I wasn't allowed to keep treating them as magic. Building the
						storage layer myself is the tuition fee.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Honest state:</span> v0.1 — reads work,
						the benchmark suite passes, and the borrow checker and I have reached
						a fragile peace (see <a href="/13/notes" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">the notes</a>).
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-5">
					<p class="text-xs text-gray-600">Rust · MIT license · 2025 — now</p>
					<a href="https://github.com/atduyar/rekv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">source ↗</a>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- Make2Game -->
			<article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.015] p-7">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-gray-100">Make2Game</h2>
					<span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 border border-white/10 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">on ice</span>
				</div>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What:</span> a 2D game engine written
						from scratch in C++ and OpenGL — Lua scripting, immediate-mode (ImGui)
						editor, batched renderer.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Why:</span> using Unity felt like driving
						an automatic. I wanted to build the transmission. It will never
						compete with Godot; it taught me more graphics programming than any
						course did.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Honest state:</span> parked while REKV
						has my evenings. The renderer works; the editor is 80% done, like all
						editors.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-5">
					<p class="text-xs text-gray-600">C++ · OpenGL · Lua · ImGui</p>
					<a href="https://github.com/atduyar/make2game" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">source ↗</a>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- Evrenomi -->
			<article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.015] p-7">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-gray-100">Evrenomi</h2>
					<span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80 border border-emerald-400/20 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">in production</span>
				</div>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What:</span> a blogging platform built as
						freelance work in 2021 — C#/.NET, obsessively optimized to a 95+
						Lighthouse score.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Honest state:</span> still online, still
						fast, still on a Linux VPS I administer. My longest-running
						production system, and the project that taught me operations.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-5">
					<p class="text-xs text-gray-600">C# / .NET · Linux VPS · 2021 — now</p>
					<a href="https://evrenomi.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">live ↗</a>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- The fleet -->
			<article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.015] p-7">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-gray-100">The Fleet</h2>
					<span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80 border border-emerald-400/20 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">always on fire somewhere</span>
				</div>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What:</span> the self-hosted
						infrastructure underneath everything else — this site, a federated
						Matrix homeserver, project hosting, backups. Debian on the servers,
						Arch on the desktop, <a href="https://github.com/atduyar/dotfiles" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">dotfiles in git</a>.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Why:</span> you write different — better —
						software when you're also the one who has to operate it.
					</p>
				</div>
				<p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-5">Linux · nginx · Docker · too much cron</p>
			</article>
		</div>

		<footer class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-white/5 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 text-xs text-gray-600">
			<a href="/13" class="hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">← home</a>
			<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/20 tracking-[0.3em] select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐰋𐰃𐰠𐰏</span>
		</footer>
	</main>

	<style is:global>
		html { background-color: #0e1014; color-scheme: dark; }
	</style>
</BaseLayout>
